1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://gw1.geneanet.org/genealogias?lang=nl;p=jose+joaquin;n=alvarez+de+toledo+y+silva '''gw1.geneanet.org....'''] ; [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jos%C3%A9_Joaqu%C3%ADn_%C3%81lvarez_de_Toledo,_18th_Duke_of_Medi
2 CONC na_Sidonia en.wikipedia.org - '''José Joaquín Álvarez de Toledo y Silva'''] ; 
2 CONT * Don José Joaquín Álvarez de Toledo y Silva, 18th Duke of Medina Sidonia, 14th Marquis of Villafranca del Bierzo, 14th Marquis of los Vélez, 12th Duke of Fernandina, 13th Marquis of Molina and 22nd Count of Niebla, Grandee of Spa
2 CONC in, Knight of the Reales Maestranzas de Caballería de Valencia and Seville, and of the Order of Alcántara (Madrid, Spain; 14 August 1826 - 15 February 1900) was a Spanish aristocrat and politician who served as Superior Chief of t
2 CONC he Palace from 1885 until his death.
2 CONT ===Background===
2 CONT * The Duke was the elder son of Pedro de Alcántara Álvarez de Toledo, 17th Duke of Medina Sidonia and María del Pilar Joaquina de Silva, fifth daughter of José Gabriel de Silva, 12th Marquis of Santa Cruz and Joaquina Téllez-Girón
2 CONC  y Pimentel, daughter of Pedro Téllez-Girón, 9th Duke of Osuna and María Josefa Pimentel, 14th Countess Duchess of Benavente. He was educated at the Theresian Military Academy, in Austro-Hungary, where his father was exiled for be
2 CONC ing a carlist sympathiser.
2 CONT ===Politics===
2 CONT * In 1847, Queen Isabella II lifted the seizure of the properties of the Medina Sidonias in Spain, and the family was able to return. The young Pepe, by then Marquis of los Vélez, started his political career, taking a seat in 185
2 CONC 2 at the Parliament of the Two Sicilies, as Prince of Paternò. He succeeded in the dukedom in 1862, and following the Restoration of the monarchy in 1874, became senator in his own right in 1875 and for the province of Cádiz in 18
2 CONC 76.
2 CONT * From 1885, he served as Superior Chief of Palace with King Alfonso XIII, and was part of the extraordinary embassy, headed by the Duke of Montpensier, sent to Russia in 1883 to represent Spain at the coronation of Tsar Alexander
2 CONC  III. He received numerous honours and decorations, including the Golden Fleece, the Collar of the Order of Charles III and the Grand Cross of the Order of the Immaculate Conception of Vila Viçosa.
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT * Medina Sidonia married his first cousin Rosalía Caro y Álvarez de Toledo, daughter of Pedro Caro, 4th Marquis of la Romana and granddaughter of Pedro Caro, 3rd Marquis of la Romana, in Erpel, Austro-Hungary, the 26 September 184
2 CONC 6. They had four children:
2 CONT # Doña María del Socorro Álvarez de Toledo (1847–1929), married Don José Maria Ortuño de Ezpeleta, 4th Duke of Castroterreño and had issue.
2 CONT # Don Alonso Álvarez de Toledo, 15th Marquis of los Vélez (1850–1897), married Doña María Trinidad Caballero, daughter of Andrés Caballero, 1st Marquis of Somosancho. Died before succeeding his father and without issue.
2 CONT # Doña Inés Álvarez de Toledo, 16th Marquise of Cazaza en África (1857–1937), married Don Fernando Ramírez de Haro, 13th Count of Bornos, and had issue.
2 CONT # Don José Joaquín Álvarez de Toledo, 19th Duke of Medina Sidonia, who succeeded in the titles of his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT 14º Velez, 17º Cazaza, Valverde, 17º Molina. 18º Dq. Medina Sidonia, 12º Fernandina, 25º Cd. Niebla, 22º conde de Caltabellotta, 17º de Caltavuturu, 18º de Coessano. Toison Oro en 1890. Caballero de Calatrava 1851. Maestrante Sevi
2 CONC lla 1848. 21º Cd. Adernó,  Montalto, Montalban. Toisón de Oro y Gran Cruz de Carlos III. Caballerizo y montero Mayor de la reina regente Mª Cristina. Senador del reino por derecho propio. Caballero de Calatrava. Gentilhombre de cá
2 CONC mara con ejercicio de Dña. Isabel, Alfonso XII y Alfonso XIII. Reconocido en Italia como príncipe de Montalbano.
2 CONT
2 CONT Don José Joaquín Álvarez de Toledo y Silva, 18th Duke of Medina Sidonia, 14th Marquis of Villafranca del Bierzo, 14th Marquis of los Vélez, 12th Duke of Fernandina, 13th Marquis of Molina and 22nd Count of Niebla, Grandee of Spain
2 CONC , Knight of the Real Maestranza de Caballería de Sevilla and of the Order of Alcántara (Madrid, Spain; 14 August 1826 - 15 February 1900) was a Spanish aristocrat and politician who served as Superior Chief of the Palace from 1885
2 CONC  until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Background
2 CONT
2 CONT The Duke was the elder son of Pedro de Alcántara Álvarez de Toledo, 13th Marquis of Villafranca and María del Pilar Joaquina de Silva, fifth daughter of José Gabriel de Silva, 12th Marquis of Santa Cruz and Joaquina Téllez-Girón y
2 CONC  Pimentel, daughter of Pedro Téllez-Girón, 9th Duke of Osuna and María Josefa Pimentel, 14th Countess Duchess of Benavente. He was educated at the Theresian Military Academy, in Austro-Hungary, where his father was exiled for bein
2 CONC g a carlist sympathiser. Politics
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1847, Queen Isabella II lifted the seizure of the properties of the Medina Sidonias in Spain, and the family was able to return. The young Pepe, by then Marquis of los Vélez, started his political career, taking a seat in 1852 
2 CONC at the Parliament of the Two Sicilies, as Prince of Paternò. He succeeded in the dukedom in 1862, and following the Restoration of the monarchy in 1874, became senator in his own right in 1875 and for the province of Cádiz in 1876
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1885, he served as Superior Chief of Palace with King Alfonso XIII, and was part of the extraordinary embassy, headed by the Duke of Montpensier, sent to Russia in 1883 to represent Spain at the coronation of Tsar Alexander I
2 CONC II. He received numerous honours and decorations, including the Golden Fleece, the Collar of the Order of Charles III and the Grand Cross of the Order of the Immaculate Conception of Vila Viçosa. Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Medina Sidonia married his first cousin Rosalía Caro y Álvarez de Toledo, daughter of Pedro Caro, 4th Marquis of la Romana and granddaughter of Pedro Caro, 3rd Marquis of la Romana, in Erpel, Austro-Hungary, the 26 September 1846.
2 CONC  They had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Doña María del Socorro Álvarez de Toledo (1847-1929), married Don José Maria Ortuño de Ezpeleta, 4th Duke of Castroterreño and had issue. Don Alonso Álvarez de Toledo, 15th Marquis of los Vélez (1850-1897), married Doña María Trin
2 CONC idad Caballero, daughter of Andrés Caballero, 1st Marquis of Somosancho. Died before succeeding his father and without issue. Doña Inés Álvarez de Toledo, 16th Marquise of Cazaza en África (1857-1937), married Don Fernando Ramírez
2 CONC  de Haro, 13th Count of Bornos, and had issue. Don José Joaquín Álvarez de Toledo, 19th Duke of Medina Sidonia, who succeeded in the titles of his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT 14º Velez, 17º Cazaza, Valverde, 17º Molina. 18º Dq. Medina Sidonia, 12º Fernandina, 25º Cd. Niebla, Toison Oro en 1890. Caballero Calatrava 1851. Maestrante Sevilla 1848. 2º Cd. Adernó,  Montalto, Montalban. Toisón de Oro y Gran 
2 CONC Cruz de Carlos III. Caballerizo y montero Mayor de la reina regente Mª Cristina. Senador del reino por derecho propio. Caballero de Calatrava. Gentilhombre de cámara con ejercicio de Dña. Isabel, Alfonso XII y Alfonso XIII.
