0 @N6000000002188436701@ NOTE On December 14, 1840 Pope Gregory XVI named Ludovico a Cardinal of the Roman Catholic Church.  However, this action was done "in pectore", which meant it was not public knowledge.  The Cardinal served as the titular Archbishop of 
1 CONC Efesco, and was a papal nuncio in Austria.  During the Papal Consistory of April 21, 1845 the Cardinals selection by the Pope was made public.  The Cardinal participated in the Papal Conclave of June 14 through June 16, 1846 which
1 CONC  elected Giovanni Maria Mastai Ferretti, Archbishop-Bishop of Imola as Pope Pius IX.
0 @N6000000002244397600@ NOTE Timid and suspicious, he was easily overruled in state and family councils.
1 CONT Thoroughly alarmed by the invasion of Giuseppe Garibaldi and the Thousand in
1 CONT May 1860, Francis, on advice of Napoleon III, capitulated to the liberals in
1 CONT his kingdom (June 25, 1860), restoring the constitution of 1848, granting
1 CONT freedom of the press, and promising fresh elections. Too late to save his
1 CONT monarchy, Francis was deposed, retiring to Rome, and later to Paris.
1 CONT Thus ended the rule of the House of Bourbon in Italy. See Victor Emmanuel II.
